      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The village hosts the Sweet Corn Festival each Labor Day weekend, a tradition that began in 1946 and draws music, parades, and square dancing.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://escapetobuckeyelake.com/directory/the-village-of-millersport/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Millersport’s founding as a port of trade on the canal positioned it as a key stop for goods moving eastward in the 19th century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
